<title>AUSTRALIA: Sipa lifts bid for Arcadia.</title>
<headline>Sipa lifts bid for Arcadia.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold explorer Sipa International Resources Ltd said on Friday that it would incrase its offer for Arcadia Minerals Ltd to seven Sipa shares and 40 cents cash for every four Arcadia shares.</p>
<p>Sipa was previously offering five of its shares for every three Arcadia shares. Arcadia owns 30 percent of the Dublin Hill gold project in Western Australia and Sipa the rest.</p>
<p>Sipa shares closed on Friday at A$0.52, down three cents, while Arcadia shares ended at A$0.84, down two.</p>
<p>The offer closes on May 23.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
